<section class="wrap section" id="get" aria-labelledby="get-title">
  <h2 id="get-title">Get riptide</h2>

  <div class="cols">
    <div>
      <h3>Needs</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Windows, with NTFS drives.</li>
        <li>Node.js.</li>
        <li>ripgrep (<code>rg</code>) on your PATH, for Search.</li>
        <li>Admin rights for the fast scan. Without them, riptide walks the folders.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3>Run</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><code>git clone https://github.com/dustinlacewell/riptide</code></li>
        <li><code>npm install</code></li>
        <li>
          <code>npm run dev</code>
          <span class="dim">Windows asks for admin rights, then riptide opens in a new console.</span>
        </li>
        <li>Open the local address it prints.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--s-6);
  }

  h3 {
    margin: var(--s-4) 0 var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--fs-title);
  }

  ul,
  ol {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--s-5);
  }

  li + li {
    margin-top: var(--s-2);
  }

  li .dim {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
  }

  ol li::marker {
    color: var(--dim);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
